    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"molecules - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\":\n    \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/molecules.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [molecules()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\n    | EdgeCase\n  description: Seven small molecules, as graphs of their atoms and bonds.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [molecules()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\n    | EdgeCase\n  description: Seven small molecules, as graphs of their atoms and bonds.\ntitle: >-\n  [molecules()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Seven small molecules, as graphs of their atoms and bonds.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nSeven small molecules, as graphs of their atoms and bonds.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/example_networks.py#L1803-L1893){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nmolecules()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\nMolecular graphs of seven well-known compounds, with a node for each atom and an edge for\neach bond. The hydrogen atoms are left out, as is usual for molecular graphs. They're\nreal molecules, chosen in pairs that look alike: ethanol and dimethyl ether have the same\natoms, as do butane and isobutane, and benzene and cyclohexane have the same shape. That\nmakes them the example for graph isomorphism, graph invariants such as the Wiener index,\nand rings.\n\nNetwork Properties:\n\n- `\"benzene\"`: 6 atoms and 6 bonds, in an aromatic ring\n- `\"cyclohexane\"`: 6 atoms and 6 single bonds, in a ring\n- `\"ethanol\"`: 3 atoms (C–C–O) and 2 bonds\n- `\"dimethyl_ether\"`: 3 atoms (C–O–C) and 2 bonds\n- `\"butane\"`: 4 carbon atoms in a chain\n- `\"isobutane\"`: 4 carbon atoms, three of them joined to the fourth\n- `\"caffeine\"`: 14 atoms (8 carbon, 4 nitrogen, 2 oxygen) and 15 bonds, in two fused rings\n- All undirected and unweighted, and each labeled by element and number, such as `\"C1\"`\n  or `\"O2\"`\n\nNode Attributes:\n\n- `element`: the chemical element, `\"C\"`, `\"N\"` or `\"O\"`\n\nEdge Attributes:\n\n- `bond`: `\"single\"`, `\"double\"` or `\"aromatic\"`\n\nWhat to Look For:\n\n- **Same shape, different molecule.** Ethanol and dimethyl ether are both three atoms in a\n  row, so `is_isomorphic()` says they match, but not with `node_attr=\"element\"`: the\n  oxygen is at the end of one and the middle of the other. Benzene and cyclohexane are\n  both rings of six carbons, and only `edge_attr=\"bond\"` tells them apart.\n- **Same atoms, different shape.** Butane and isobutane both have four carbons, but one is\n  a chain and the other branched, so they're not isomorphic.\n- **The Wiener index.** The sum of the distances between all pairs of atoms is 10 for\n  butane and 9 for the more compact isobutane. Wiener introduced the index in 1947 to\n  predict boiling points, which are lower for more compact molecules.\n- **Two rings, or one.** Caffeine's rings have 5 and 6 atoms, and\n  `minimum_cycle_basis()` finds those two, but `cycle_basis()` can return the 9-atom\n  ring around the outside of both in place of one of them. The girth is 5.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict[str, Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The molecules, keyed by name: `\"benzene\"`, `\"cyclohexane\"`, `\"ethanol\"`,\n    `\"dimethyl_ether\"`, `\"butane\"`, `\"isobutane\"` and `\"caffeine\"`.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nDraw caffeine, colored by element, with its bonds labeled:\n\n::: {#daf273ce .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ncaffeine = ec.molecules()[\"caffeine\"]\n\ncaffeine.plot(\n    color_by=\"element\", label_by=\"label\", edge_label_by=\"bond\", seed=1\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d